---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Practice — Ruijie Wu" description="Psychotherapy, embodied approaches and dance movement practice.">
  <section class="page-intro container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Practice / 02</span>
    <h1>Making room<br /><em>for experience.</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">Different ways of approaching experience, held with curiosity, respect and care.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container practice-paths">
    <a class="practice-path" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}practice/psychotherapy/`}><span class="number">01</span><div><h2>Psychotherapy</h2><p>Emotional life, relationships, grief, trauma, identity and meaning-making.</p><span class="path-action">Explore this approach ↗</span></div></a>
    <a class="practice-path" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}practice/embodied/`}><span class="number">02</span><div><h2>Embodied approaches</h2><p>Sensation, gesture, movement and the knowledge that emerges through the body.</p><span class="path-action">Explore this approach ↗</span></div></a>
    <a class="practice-path" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}practice/dance-movement/`}><span class="number">03</span><div><h2>Dance &amp; creative movement</h2><p>Movement, rhythm, space and group processes as resources for expression and discovery.</p><span class="path-action">Explore this approach ↗</span></div></a>
  </section>
  <section class="practice-note"><div class="container practice-note-grid"><span class="eyebrow">A collaborative process</span><div class="prose"><p>Therapeutic work is not about providing standard answers. It begins by understanding what is happening and finding a way of working that respects each person's circumstances, wishes and pace.</p><p>Words, images, bodily awareness or movement may all have a place, depending on the person and the context.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}contact/`}>Get in touch <span>↗</span></a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>